e.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2F0a7224d9-745b-49d0-b8ba-883413c90a76-image.png?alt=media\"/></p>\n<p>Thus, the hybridisation of the central atom remains unchanged in ${NH}_{3} \\to {NH}_{4}^{+}$.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6f3e6f2d672f7b81571"},{"id":51003,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Among the following, the species with identical bond order are","options":["$CO$ and ${O}_{2}^{2 -}$","${O}_{2}^{-}$ and $CO$","${O}_{2}^{2 -}$ and ${B}_{2}$","$CO$ and ${N}_{2}^{+}$"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>The bond order can be calculated<br />\nas</p> <p>$B . O = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left({N}_{b} - {N}_{a}\\right)</p> <p>Where, ${N}_{b} =$ Electrons in bonding orbitals ${N}_{a} =$ Electrons in anti bonding orbitals.<br />\n(a) $CO$ and ${O}_{2}^{2 -}$</p> <p>The electronic configuration of $CO$ (14) is</p> <p>$\\sigma1s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}1s^{2}\\sigma2s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}2s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}2{p}_z^{2}\\pi2{p}_x^{2}\\pi2p^{2}y$</p> <p>$∴ B . O = $\\dfrac{1}{2} (10 - 4 ) = \\dfrac{6}{2} =3$</p> <p>(b) ${O}_{2}^{-}$ and $CO$</p> <p>The electronic configuration of ${0}_{2}^{-} ( 17 )$ is</p> <p>$\\sigma1s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}1s^{2}\\sigma2s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}2s^{2}\\sigma2{p}_z^{2}\\pi2{p}_x^{2}$</p> <p>$\\pi2{p}_y^{2}{\\pi}^{*}2{p}_x^{2}{\\pi}^{*}2{p}_y^{1}$</p>\n$B . O = \\dfrac{1}{2} (10 - 7 ) = \\dfrac{3}{2} =1 . 5$\n<p>$B . O .$ of $CO$ is $3$</p> <p>[as calculated in option (a)]</p> <p>(c) $B . O .$. of ${O}_{2}^{2 -}$ is 1</p> <p>[as calculated in option (a)]</p> <p>The electronic configuration of ${B}_{2} ( 10 )$ is</p> <p>$\\sigma1s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}1s^{2}\\sigma2s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}2s^{2}\\pi2{p}_x^{1}\\pi2{p}_y^{1}$</p>\n$B . O = \\dfrac{1}{2} [6 - 4 ] = \\dfrac{2}{2} =1$\n<p>(d) $B . O$. of $CO$ is $3$</p> <p>[as calculated in option (a)]</p> <p>Electronic configuration of ${N}_{2}^{+}$ ($13$) is</p> <p>$\\sigma1s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}1s^{2}\\sigma2s^{2}{&#963;}^{*}2s^{2}\\pi2{p}_x^{2}\\pi2{p}_y^{2}\\sigma2{p}_z^{1}$</p>\n$B . O = \\dfrac{1}{2} [9 - 4 ] = \\dfrac{5}{2} =2 . 5$\n<p>Thus, option (c) is correct.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SA)","_marksId":"614da3fec9e7631d376607ff"},{"id":51004,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The shape of $\\mathrm{SCl}_{4}$ is best described as a","options":["square","tetrahedron","square pyramid","see-saw"],"answer":3,"solution":"$\\mathrm{SCl}_{4} \\Rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{ b}. \\mathrm{p}+1 \\ell. \\mathrm{p}$\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252Fe6ogNOmduKJLe2mFTixB5jqgaPrK-zNFRJm04gublBw.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fe6ogNOmduKJLe2mFTixB5jqgaPrK-zNFRJm04gublBw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fe6ogNOmduKJLe2mFTixB5jqgaPrK-zNFRJm04gublBw.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2016 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21307d4254b2ee8d9da"},{"id":51005,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The numbers of lone pairs and bond pairs in hydrazine are, respectively","options":["2 and 4","2 and 6","2 and 5","1 and 5"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\quad$ HYDRAZINE $\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4}$\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%25